    <briefdescription>
<para>Vertex object representing an individual resident component of a network. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Vertices contain their own state vectors, local dynamics, and noise, and form the nodes of the network topology. Coupling between vertices is made explicit by edges.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="warning"><para>Destroying a vertex also destroys all edges coupled to that vertex, invalidating any pointers to those edges. Any channels used by the vertex remain unaffected.</para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="group__vertex__creation_1gaec4b6881830464281fc35817e96bfaf3" kindref="member">ndxlCreateVertex</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="group__edge__creation_1ga64a610b6a899977bbf5722ca30f92114" kindref="member">ndxlCreateEdge</ref> </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
